{
  "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
  "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Deferred payments under section 1325(a)(5)(B)(ii) must equal the present value of the collateral. Historically present value has been an objective concept equalling the real interest rate and inflation, which is the time value of money."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: When you say traditionally it's been understood to mean real interest rate plus time value of money, it means real interest rate for the particular lender. Isn't -- I mean, the -- the interest rate that is given to different lenders is not always the same."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Where do you get the principle that all secured creditors have to be treated equally? Where does -- where does that appear?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, why isn't that a valid distinction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Salmons",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SALMONS: Your Honor, if -- if this Court believes that risks of nonpayment need to be taken into account, then we submit that the best way to do that is to start with a market indicator such as the prime rate that captures the time value of money and the risk of inflation and then -- then allow -- and -- and some risk of nonpayment, and then allow the bankruptcy court, which -- which, by the way, has just made a determination under 1325(a)(6) about the likelihood that -- that the payments will be made."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Bankruptcy Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the bankruptcy court, which -- which, by the way, has just made a determination under 1325(a)(6) about the likelihood that -- that the payments will be made."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRUNSTAD: Yes, Your Honor. There -- there is one study that suggests that, but I must -- I must add that -- that there are other studies that say that the successful completion rate is as low as 3 percent in some jurisdictions. Some 97 percent of chapter 13 fail."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Would it satisfy you if we said this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But no. But does what I say satisfy you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, the secured creditor in the chapter 13 cramdown context is not trying to make any profit. It's simply trying to mitigate against the enormous losses that it suffers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But it seems pretty obvious if it's a higher rate, there are going to be more defaults."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, not necessarily, Your Honor, for this reason. Because the debtor makes -- the -- the debtor does not make payments directly to creditors under the chapter 13 plan. The debtor makes payments to the chapter 13 trustee as a dispersing agent, and the chapter 13 trustee then distributes the money."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15f8483fa7a92f20849e03b6ebf439491ed58c94652356ba359396f7036094bc",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15f8483fa7a9-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: Thank you, Ms. Harper. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-02-1016",
      "confidence": 1.0,
